# Vercel ignore — repo root.
#
# Background: the deploy script (web/scripts/deploy-prod.sh) runs vercel
# from the repo root because the Vercel project's Root Directory setting
# is `web/` (running vercel from web/ would resolve to <repo>/web/web/).
# Without this ignore, vercel uploads the entire repo — including data/
# (multi-GB cached PDFs), supabase/, src/, etc. — and Vercel rejects
# deploys whose source tree exceeds 15000 files OR several GB.
#
# Vercel's Root Directory project setting still controls what becomes the
# build context. This ignore just keeps non-web/ paths out of the upload
# in the first place so we don't hit upload limits.
#
# CRITICAL: leading slashes are required to anchor patterns to the repo
# root. Without them, gitignore-syntax (which .vercelignore uses) treats
# patterns as unanchored — `src/` then matches BOTH `/src/` AND
# `/web/src/`, silently breaking the Next.js build because the entire
# app source tree disappears. This was discovered the hard way on
# 2026-05-22 when the first guarded deploy succeeded the upload step but
# Vercel then failed with "Couldn't find any `pages` or `app` directory."

# Backend Python pipeline + tests + data (root-level only)
/src/
/tests/
/data/
/mcp/
/scripts/

# Database migrations + Supabase CLI state
/supabase/

# Internal docs (not needed for the build) — root-level only
/docs/
/JOURNAL.md
/LICENSE

# Claude worktrees, AI artifacts, local state
/.claude/
/.sfdx/
/tmp/

# Python build artifacts — these can appear anywhere; unanchored is fine
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.pytest_cache/
htmlcov/
.coverage
*.egg-info/

# Top-level config not needed at deploy time
/pytest.ini
/requirements.txt
/requirements-dev.txt

# Local environment files never belong in a deployment upload. Examples are
# also build-irrelevant, so exclude the full root + web env-file families.
/.env*
/web/.env*

# Vercel internal state — anywhere
.vercel/

# Local dependency/build output — anywhere. These explicit patterns keep the
# upload set aligned with deploy-prod.sh's quota-cap estimator; do not rely on
# undocumented CLI defaults.
node_modules/
.next/

# Logs — anywhere
*.log
